{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960299-armageddon","id":960299,"title":"Armageddon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-30T01:34:22-07:00","id":960299,"title":"Armageddon","content":"What would the world be like if the absolute worst scenarios from end of the world Time of Judgement happened from the &quot;BIG 3&quot; titles of WoD at the exact same time. Would society collapse, civilization as we k ow be smashed, and the supernatural of the world be the governing bodies? Cities in ruin and being vampiric fiefdoms. Garou openly running free range hunting the Wyrm monstrosities. Technocractic states protecting humanity. Possibilities. <br /> <br /> Thoughts. Ideas. Let me know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T02:25:07-07:00","id":960313,"title":"","content":"The absolute worst scenarios from the big three all at once? How are you defining 'worst'? Does the universe as we know it ceasing to exist qualify as good or bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T02:32:22-07:00","id":960316,"title":"","content":"Worst is kind of subjective... worst for humanity? Worst for the supernaturals in question? Worst spread around as evenly as possible?<br /> <br /> <br /> Though everything you're suggesting is... tame by many of the ToJ books. A combination of them could easily leave Earth a life-less rock with nothing on it, all the supernaturals extinct, and even the great powers like Caine, Lilith, Luna, Gaia, the Trait, and so on dead.<br /> <br /> Consider that one of the Apocalypse scenarios <i>starts</i> with Rorg (the Celestine spirit of the Asteroid Belt) deciding that Gaia needs a reboot and throws a gigantic asteroid at Earth with the intent of causing a mass extinction event, but ends up tossing one so big, that Luna has to physically move the moon in the way of it to avoid Earth being obliterated, which results in both the asteroid and the moon exploding and raining the shrapnel into us with as devastating results as you can imagine that would cause... and then shit gets worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T04:57:27-07:00","id":960356,"title":"","content":"The Rorg scenario would require Ceres as the projectile (the moon is hard to destroy because it is really, really large) and would end up with everything on the Earth being wiped out either way. For the human species, anything that happened afterwards would be academic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:52:40-07:00","id":960544,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Hell on Earth&quot; scenario results in the Nephandi Lords being summoned to Earth, so I think that one has fair claim on the title of worst for the Mage game. Everyone who didn't die would <b>wish</b> they had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T11:21:12-07:00","id":960563,"title":"","content":"The closest i have seen, was someone who wanted to start a 'day after the apocalypse game, using werewolf wild west as a sort of backdrop;.. BUT never got passed the planning stage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:46:07-07:00","id":960648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960299-armageddon?p=960544#post960544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Hell on Earth&quot; scenario results in the Nephandi Lords being summoned to Earth, so I think that one has fair claim on the title of worst for the Mage game. Everyone who didn't die would <b>wish</b> they had.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though scenarios like Rorg's Claw kind of include this.<br /> <br /> Hell on Earth is probably the worst (or tied for the worst if Voormas wins his scenario) if we're just using Mage. A Whimper Not a Bang, is actually probably the worst Mage scenario in combination with the Gehenna/Apocalypse ones, because it means mages are taken completely out of the picture. No mages forming pocket dimensions as lifeboats for life to hide from the destruction. No Technocracy war fleets in the Umbra fighting back the forces of the Wyrm. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T16:31:14-07:00","id":960737,"title":"","content":"I personally haven't read the ToJ books. But I think a crossover post Armageddon type scenario would be very interesting to run. Where humanity knows that all the Splats exist and that the splats now have a opportunity to operate freely now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T17:28:42-07:00","id":960753,"title":"","content":"It can certainly be done. It's just that most of the ToJ scenarios that allow it are the &quot;nice&quot; ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:54:34-07:00","id":960816,"title":"","content":"By most definitions, the total non-existence of the cosmos would count as worst, and that's a potential Mage outcome.* So if the 'worst' scenario of the three big ones come to pass, there can be no 'after the end' game as the concepts of 'after', 'the', and 'end' all rely on there being time and space - neither of which will remain in any recognizable form.<br /> <br /> (* It's actually the <i>best</i> outcome of the setting, which is why I asked earlier about the definition of worst.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T20:12:34-07:00","id":960820,"title":"","content":"Voormas winning is actually one of the better outcomes, really. I mean, at least you get free immortality out of the package, even if you kill most capacity for change and creativity. Infinitely better than just dying or being enslaved by cosmic horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T22:52:03-07:00","id":960898,"title":"","content":"The loss of capacity for change is, in a mage cosmology, actually one of the worst possible outcomes. The purpose of the human being is not to live forever, but to affect change. Voormas's victory represents one of the greatest possible perversions of that purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T08:44:24-07:00","id":961072,"title":"","content":"Besides what Voormas is offering is not &quot;immortality&quot;, because being immortal implies you live,in Voormas new world you don't live, you just exist.<br /> <br /> Peoples in Voormas' world would simply be not alive neither dead, you would simply exist in an unending moment of perfect stasis, because nothing new can happen and nothing can end, there would be no new moments, no new toughts, no new actions, no new nothing, Time would simply stop.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:07:28-07:00","id":961123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960299-armageddon?p=960316#post960316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worst is kind of subjective... worst for humanity? Worst for the supernaturals in question? Worst spread around as evenly as possible?<br /> <br /> <br /> Though everything you're suggesting is... tame by many of the ToJ books. A combination of them could easily leave Earth a life-less rock with nothing on it, all the supernaturals extinct, and even the great powers like Caine, Lilith, Luna, Gaia, the Trait, and so on dead.<br /> <br /> Consider that one of the Apocalypse scenarios <i>starts</i> with Rorg (the Celestine spirit of the Asteroid Belt)</div> </div> </div> </div>Rorg is an Incarna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T19:31:03-07:00","id":961357,"title":"","content":"Maybe it did happen. Maybe they all happened. Maybe a new cycle started and we all forgot. <br /> Well.. most of us... Wellll some of us. Welllllll a few at any rate.<br /> Maybe some remember it in blurry dreams of angels and demons and heroes and monsters.<br /> Maybe at the end of the old world, there was a new God... and she said &quot;Let there be light.&quot;<br /> Maybe....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T05:31:26-07:00","id":961599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960299-armageddon?p=960544#post960544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Hell on Earth&quot; scenario results in the Nephandi Lords being summoned to Earth, so I think that one has fair claim on the title of worst for the Mage game. Everyone who didn't die would <b>wish</b> they had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, Thailand doesn't seem so bad. &quot;<i>When asked, she happily confesses she was once a priestess-whore of Babylon. The Harlot Empress sits upon an undulating throne of intertwined human bodies on orgiastic celebration, deep within her citadel within in what used to be Bangkok.</i>&quot; Granted, it might not be that rosy, but at the very least it beats living in areas influenced by the other Aswadim. (Or Voormas) There are even people willing to give their life for the Harlot Empress.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/960299-armageddon#post960299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would society collapse, civilization as we k ow be smashed, and the supernatural of the world be the governing bodies? Cities in ruin and being vampiric fiefdoms. Garou openly running free range hunting the Wyrm monstrosities. Technocractic states protecting humanity. Possibilities.<br /> Thoughts. Ideas. Let me know</div> </div> </div> </div>The ability to form a stable fiefdoms containing humans - where they wouldn't all be led to crematoriums (or some equivalent) sooner or later - would be key to winning such a struggle, I'd say. Pentex, together with Black Spirals (who are noted as treating their kinfolk good enough) might be the best in it, considering that they are human. Mages as well.<br /> I can very well imagine some 4th and lower generation vampires quickly burning themselves out, whether through mass killing or humans dying due to neglect and sheer despair. (or being killed when they rebel or try to flee en masse.)<br /> <br /> Transcendent Antediluvians - like Lasombra, Ennoia, Malkav and Tzimisce - could be a problem when they would be hitting cities or countries, others following in their wake.<br /> Mages could ward the cities they protect. Or possibly whole continents and larger islands. Japan, UK and Australia could be bunkered up like this. Japan would be Technocracy - or Five Elemental Dragons; Australia would be a haven for Garou &amp; Mages; and UK would be an alliance of Cainites and Mages. Of course the Mages might find themselves Blood Bound and Dominated in short time; or possibly not - when your survival is at stake constantly, muddling the minds of those that are responsible for massive warding rituals is not the wisest thing.<br /> <br /> Also, in a world on the edge of ending there would be so many outright hostile people..Cainites could have an understanding with allied Mages to only drain criminals, enemies and traitors. Imagine England openly ruled by the NWO, and if cameras see you commit any serious crime you are brought to the rack within 24 hours. Suspicions can be confirmed with True Magick or Thaumaturgy, so the court's verdicts are never wrong. And cities &amp; towns are warded so that nobody can <i>leave</i>. For their own safety, of course. When they is perfect justice, what do you have to fear unless you deserve punishment? And of course it it innately suspicious that anyone would want to leave any of England's cities, considering how prosperous and safe they are because of joint efforts of the New Government and a number of reclusive, shadowy philanthropists.<br /> Something akin to <i>The Minority's Report </i>could be done in which suspected criminals are identified by Technocrats and taken for processing. If they are deemed as possible to redeem, they are made into ghouls and drafted to make-up for the crimes they didn't commit.<br /> Scotland would be independent after Verbena raised a desperate ward barring |Order of Hermes| from interfering with the fate of Scotland. It works against both Clan Tremere and (sadly) Hermetics, and causes aging in any Hermetic who tries to interfere. The UK Technocracy stopped trying to absorb Scotland after they almost killed their Tremere allies. (the ward hit Tremeres because they essentially knew what their allies were doing, which counts as supports which counts as interfering)<br /> <br /> Pentex would dominate North America and would have understanding(s) with the Sabbat. The fact that their Mockery Breeds incite Delirium could be key.<br /> <br /> The Changing Breeds inciting Delirium in the weak-willed would make them wanted allies, servants and slaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-01-2016, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}